;; Declared fence exemptions (ADR-0158, review-4 register row D8-2,
;; author ruling R4-Q4 (a)).
;;
;; R4-Q4 (a) gates `bare-on-README+SETUP = 0`. Measuring the four fences
;; that rule costs found that they are not four cheap ones: two teach
;; commands that CANNOT be run by a checker without lying about what
;; they do -- `sudo apt install` mutates the machine, and a fresh-clone
;; `git clone` of this repo over the network is not a check of this
;; tree. A third teaches a deliberately real-time viewing rate.
;;
;; The honest instrument is a third disposition. A command fence on the
;; reader path is `exercised` (some bin/ script re-runs it verbatim,
;; `exercised-sources.edn`), or `exempt` (a row HERE, with a reason a
;; human wrote), or `bare` -- and bare is what the gate forbids. A new
;; fence is bare by default, so the ratchet holds: nobody can add an
;; unexercised front-door fence without either exercising it or writing
;; down why it cannot be.
;;
;; Rows are anchored by (:file, :first-command) rather than by line
;; number, so ordinary editing above a fence does not silently retarget
;; an exemption. `ehrt.docs-tooling.front-door-fence-gate-test` asserts
;; every row matches a live fence, so a row cannot outlive the fence it
;; excuses.
;;
;; :covered-by is optional and names a script that exercises the same
;; commands somewhere they CAN be run. It is documentation, not a
;; substitute for the reason.

[{:file "README.md"
  :first-command "bin/ehrt corpus generate sim --seed 5 --patients 200 \\"
  :reason
  "Teaches a real-time viewing rate on purpose: `--board 60 --rate 60`
   is 'an hour of hospital time per minute', which is what the section
   is about. Run verbatim against a 200-patient, ten-year clinic-decade
   corpus it is weeks of wallclock, so no checker can run it as taught
   without changing the one flag the prose exists to show."
  :covered-by "bin/demo-exerciser-clinic-decade"
  :witness {:adr "ADR-0158" :date "2026-08-19"}}

 {:file "SETUP.md"
  :first-command "sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y openjdk-21-jdk git"
  :reason
  "Installs system packages as root and runs a downloaded installer
   under sudo. Exercising it would mutate the machine running the
   checker; on a machine that already satisfies it, the run proves
   nothing about the instruction."
  :witness {:adr "ADR-0158" :date "2026-08-19"}}

 {:file "SETUP.md"
  :first-command "git clone https://github.com/pragsmike/ehr-testing-tools.git"
  :reason
  "Clones this repo from GitHub into a new directory. A checker already
   running inside a clone cannot perform a fresh clone as a check OF
   that clone, and the network fetch is not a property of this tree. The
   post-clone half of the ladder, `clojure -M:poly version` and `clojure
   -M:poly check`, is what `make test`'s own first line runs every push."
  :covered-by "Makefile target `test`"
  :witness {:adr "ADR-0158" :date "2026-08-19"}}]
